# banded_body.xlsx -- FROZEN EXPECTATION.
# A reading of the openpyxl-authored fixture against plan 05.
# Corrected ONLY when that reading was wrong -- never edited to chase an FSA1 regression.
#
# Derived by hand: the six rows are dense, so occupancy cuts ONE block A1:B6. Rows 2, 4 and 6
# carry the shade and rows 1, 3 and 5 carry nothing, so the modal background is UNSET and no `td`
# rule is written. The shaded lines are {2,4,6}, which is exactly the class of 1..=6 congruent to
# 0 modulo 2 -- not merely inside it -- so the three row rules collapse to the one periodic rule.
file: Report/A1:B6
|North	10
|South	20
|East	30
|West	40
|Inland	50
|Coast	60
|@scope {
|  tr:nth-child(2n) td { background-color: #f2f2f2 }
|}
